{
  "name": "aom_doublepass_fixed",
  "description": "Rb-87 780 nm AOM double-pass (fixed: return ghost dumped) in cat-eye configuration (after PyOpticL's doublepass module). Fiber-coupled light is cleaned up by a HWP + PBS, diffracted by an 80 MHz Isomet AOM, retro-reflected through a f=75 mm lens / QWP / mirror cat-eye so the +1 order re-enters the AOM and is diffracted again (+160 MHz total, beam pointing independent of RF frequency). The double-passed QWP turns H into V so the PBS reflects the return beam into the output fiber. The forward 0th order is caught by a razor-blade dump before the retro mirror, and the un-diffracted part of the return pass (a ghost 0.85\u00b0 off axis) is blocked before the output fiber.",
